    "result_text": "All tests pass. Let me verify the full compile is clean and summarize what changed.\n\nThe implementation is complete and the suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing, including the new `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**1. OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 the DTOs are generated from this at build time:\n- Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` string properties to `OwnerFields` (both normal read/write fields, so they're accepted on input and returned on reads).\n- Reworded `address` to document it as the backward-compatible flat input / composed output.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, so a structured-only owner passes bean validation (otherwise the generated `@NotNull` would 400 before reaching the controller).\n\n**2. `Owner` model** \u2014 added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters. MapStruct maps them automatically (matching names) in both directions.\n\n**3. `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 the core logic:\n- Normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and the flat `address` (each via the existing `normalizeAddress`).\n- Prefers structured when `addressLine1` is non-blank; otherwise falls back to the flat address.\n- Composes the stored/returned `address` as normalized `addressLine1` + (a single space + normalized `addressLine2` when present) via a new `composeAddress` helper.\n- Requires an address in **either** form plus city (contract stays backward-compatible; minimal flat owners still accepted).\n- Stores the normalized structured lines on the owner (null when the flat form was used).\n\n**4. DB schemas** \u2014 added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), placed at the end. The hsqldb `data.sql` uses positional inserts, so I appended two `NULL`s to each seed-owner row (h2/postgres use explicit-column inserts and were unaffected).\n\nThe two new tests confirm: structured input is normalized (`\"10 king st\"` \u2192 `addressLine1` = `\"10 KING STREET\"`, composed `address` = `\"10 KING STREET\"`), and the flat `address` form still succeeds.",
